# Light-curve CSV files (Kyoto, Kiso, Fukushima)

This directory contains the reduced, normalized occultation light curves used in the manuscript:
Arimatsu, K., et al., “Detection of an atmosphere on a trans-Neptunian object beyond Pluto”, Nature Astronomy, in revision.

The light curves were produced from the raw movie/cube data (see 'movie_data/' and its README for raw-file formats and instrument-specific timing notes). Each CSV file provides time-series photometry of the occulted star around the event.

## Files in this directory

| Station     | CSV file name              | N (rows) | MJD range (UTC)                        | Approx. UTC coverage (start–end)           |
|-------------|----------------------------|----------|----------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| Kyoto       | `lightcurve_Kyoto.csv`     | 580      | 60319.54761314815 – 60319.55444662037  | 2024-01-10 13:08:33.776 – 13:18:24.188 UTC |
| Kiso        | `lightcurve_Kiso.csv`      | 360      | 60319.549578101854 – 60319.55169814815 | 2024-01-10 13:11:23.548 – 13:14:26.720 UTC |
| Fukushima   | `lightcurve_Fukushima.csv` | 183      | 60319.55005473 – 60319.5510869         | 2024-01-10 13:12:04.728 – 13:13:33.908 UTC |

Cadences are computed from the median time step in each file; occasional gaps can exist due to dropped/flagged frames.

## CSV format

All files are comma-separated values (CSV) with a single header row and three columns:

### Column 1: `MJD`
Time stamp in Modified Julian Date (days). The times are the UTC time stamps used in our analysis pipeline for each exposure/frame.
Instrument-specific timing definitions/corrections (e.g., GPS synchronization, sensor readout timing, PPS-based corrections) are described in the 'movie_data/' README. Users should refer to that document if they wish to reconstruct timestamps directly from the raw movies/cubes.

### Column 2: `Scaled_flux`
Dimensionless, normalized flux of the occulted star after differential photometry and normalization to the unocculted (out-of-occultation) flux level.
Values are expected to scatter around ~1 outside the occultation features.

### Column 3: `Error`
1σ uncertainty of `Scaled_flux` for each time sample (dimensionless). These uncertainties are intended for weighted fitting and χ² calculations.

## Practical notes

1. These CSV light curves are the recommended inputs for reproducing the figures and atmospheric fits in the manuscript. They already reflect the photometric calibration and time-stamping conventions used in the analysis.
2. If you need to regenerate the light curves from raw data, use the raw files under 'movie_data/' together with the instrument/timing notes provided there.

